finding('CONTENT-01','Component salvage requires an unavailable wrench','normal acquisition blocker','11 component types are populated from role sets but ordinary dismount/remount requires wrench or tool_wrench; neither is registered or supplied by any item, loot, recipe, authored home content, live generator grant or pickup. Component item forms consequently have no demonstrated normal inventory acquisition.',[c('Core/Session/RunSession.WorkAction.cs','TryWorkActionInteract','bool hasWrench'),c('Core/Systems/Inventory/ItemDefs.cs','LoadDefinitions'),d('components/component_catalog.json','components')])
finding('CONTENT-02','Carried component forms lack inventory definitions','latent disconnected schema defect','All 11 component item_form IDs are absent from merged ItemDefs. Unknown inventory weights default to zero, max stack to99 and category empty. Component catalog mass is never used by InventoryState; deposit-all excludes empty category. Normal player acquisition is currently wrench-blocked, so this is not presented as a normal-play zero-weight exploit.',[c('Core/Systems/Inventory/ItemDefs.cs','WeightEach'),c('Core/Systems/Inventory/ItemDefs.cs','MaxStack'),c('Core/Systems/Inventory/CargoTransfer.cs','HAULABLE_CATEGORIES'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.WorkAction.cs','TickWorkAction','InventoryState.AddItem(form, 1)')])
finding('CONTENT-03','Most recipe inputs have no supported source','normal content availability gap','Even a permissive upper bound that grants access to all9 loot tables, all component role candidates and both crop products leaves42/62 authored recipes blocked by17 ingredient IDs.31/115 registered items have no enumerated acquisition edge at all. This denominator is not a runtime completion rate.7 deconstruction recipes remain among the20 source-feasible recipes; at most13/55 non-deconstruction recipes survive this source-only upper bound.',[d('recipes/recipe_definitions.json','recipes'),d('materials/material_definitions.json','materials'),d('items/loot_tables.json','generic_crate')],'Upper-bound static closure ignores quantity, room geometry, tool, station, tier, class progression and finite depletion; cannot overstate availability as reachability.')
finding('CONTENT-04','Tier upgrades are discarded by spatial craft precheck','normal UI gate defect','The only2 recipes with nonzero station tier (craft_sensor_module tier1 and craft_thruster_nozzle tier2) are listed and prechecked with omitted stationTier parameter, default0. TryCraftRecipe rejects before BeginCraft can use station.EffectiveTier. Both recipes also have unavailable ingredients, so this is an independent latent gate behind the source blocker.',[c('Core/Session/Interactables/CraftingStation.cs','TryCraftRecipe','CraftingState.CanCraft(recipeId, InventoryState)'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.Crafting.cs','ListStationRecipeEntries','CraftingState.ListRecipeEntries(stationKind, InventoryState, skill)'),c('Core/Systems/Crafting/CraftingState.cs','BeginCraft','long stTier = station.EffectiveTier()'),d('recipes/recipe_definitions.json','craft_sensor_module'),d('recipes/recipe_definitions.json','craft_thruster_nozzle')])
finding('CONTENT-05','Recipe knowledge and skill books are disconnected','disconnected/legacy systems','RecipeKnowledgeState exists only as a model and CraftingState optional argument; session creates no instance, passes no knowledge, emits no LearnFromBook/CodeX/RegisterDismantle and saves no knowledge summary.61 recipes author starter and1 book; the sole book recipe has no knowledge_book_id.12 skill books are not registered inventory items and no non-test caller invokes GrantXpFromBook.2 advanced skill nodes require those books or matching codex IDs that normal catalog does not grant.',[c('Core/Systems/Crafting/RecipeKnowledgeState.cs','LearnFromBook'),c('Core/Systems/Crafting/CraftingState.cs','CanCraft'),c('Core/Systems/Progression/PlayerProgressionState.cs','GrantXpFromBook'),d('player/skill_tree.json','welding_mastery'),d('player/skill_tree.json','biomatter_diagnostics')])
finding('CONTENT-06','Claimed vessels do not inherit home services','special identity/coverage gap','BuildCraftingStations and BuildProductionStations clear current stations then return whenever AwayFromStart or home unavailable. Boarding a secured claimed home-member sets AwayFromStart if target != HomeShip and rebuilds both. Thus ownership, repaired power and shelter on reclaimed non-home vessels do not instantiate station crafting or production; portable craft/wound treatment still work. No home relocation/promotion workflow was found.',[c('Core/Session/RunSession.Crafting.cs','BuildCraftingStations','if (AwayFromStart || HomeShip'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.Crafting.cs','BuildProductionStations','void BuildProductionStations'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.HomeExtension.cs','ActivateBoardedContext','CurrentShip=target;AwayFromStart=target!=HomeShip;')])
finding('CONTENT-07','Medbay surgery depends on source-less gauze','normal acquisition blocker','Medbay surgery requires medical_gauze, but gauze has no loot/recipe/production/pickup/authored source. The medbay skill bypass itself is a design choice. Normal wound bandaging instead accepts bandage_kit and normal direct healing accepts field_medkit; those2 types have current generated medical-room supplies.',[c('Core/Session/RunSession.Crafting.cs','TryMedbaySurgery','GetQuantity("medical_gauze")'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.cs','BANDAGE_ITEM_IDS'),c('Core/Procgen/GameplaySliceBuilder.cs','Build','"field_medkit"')])
finding('CONTENT-08','Full item stacks consume finite loot containers','intentional loss policy with irreversible depletion','LootContainer marks searched after attempting grants even if AddItem accepts zero or only a partial stack. It does not retain contents for retry. Looted IDs are persisted, so finite maintenance/medical/crew supplies lost to stack overflow stay lost on revisit/load. This is explicitly commented policy, not a weight-cap bug: InventoryState weight is soft capped.',[c('Core/Session/Interactables/LootContainer.cs','TryInteract','Searching consumes the container'),c('Core/Session/Interactables/LootContainer.cs','GrantAuthoredContents','long added = InventoryState.AddItem(itemId, qty)'),c('Core/Systems/Travel/ShipInstance.cs','GetSummary','result["looted_containers"]'),c('Core/Systems/Inventory/InventoryState.cs','AddItem')])
finding('CONTENT-09','Queued craft completion bypasses ingredient consumption','disconnected legacy path','FinishCraft starts the next queued recipe and changes active recipe without ConsumeIngredients, skill/tier/knowledge or output-space checks. No live UI/Session call to EnqueueCraft exists, so do not classify as reachable free-craft exploit.',[c('Core/Systems/Crafting/CraftingState.cs','FinishCraft','Auto-start next queued recipe'),c('Core/Systems/Crafting/CraftingState.cs','EnqueueCraft')])
finding('CONTENT-10','Generic structural work lacks continuous site validation','normal candidate requiring runtime','TickWorkAction continuously checks site/range/LOS only for secure_connection, commission_home_propulsion and cut_web_attachment. Generic cutting/prying/component work can continue with held input after moving away and completes against current ModuleIntegrityMap/ComponentPlacementState. The component variants are additionally blocked by missing wrench. Parent should verify normal structural cut case before promoting severity.',[c('Core/Session/RunSession.WorkAction.cs','TickWorkAction','if(WorkActionDriver.Work.ActionId=="secure_connection"'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.WorkAction.cs','TryWorkActionInteract'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.WorkAction.cs','ApplyWorkYieldsToInventoryState')])
finding('CONTENT-11','Starting class levels and uniform fabrication checks','design choice/functional specialization gap','All spatial station recipes use fabrication rather than station-specific cooking/pharmacology. Engineer/mechanic start fabrication1, all other9 classes0. Portable recipes skip skill gating and use fabrication only for quality. Initial shuttle nav_linkage repair2 is immediately available to engineer/mechanic/scientist (3/11;3/8 base), home propulsion repair4 to mechanic (1/11). This is not evidence of class deadlock: objectives award repairXP, repair points train, hub bonus can add repair1.',[c('Core/Session/Interactables/CraftingStation.cs','PlayerSkill','GetSkillLevel("fabrication")'),d('player/classes.json','classes'),d('ship_systems/systems.json','nav_linkage'),d('work_actions/work_action_catalog.json','commission_home_propulsion'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.Objectives.cs','OnInteractableCompleted','TrainingEventBus?.Emit("repair_full_system"')])
finding('CONTENT-12','Reload disables hold requirement for active work','normal candidate requiring runtime','RunSnapshotAssembler saves active/interrupted WorkActionState and RunSession.Save restores it but sets _workRequiresHold=false regardless HoldToWork settings. A current held structural action can therefore resume progress after reload without held interact; parent must verify normal start/save/reload sequence.',[c('Core/Session/RunSnapshotAssembler.cs','WorkActionSummary','if (s.WorkActionDriver != null'),c('Core/Session/RunSession.Save.cs','Apply','_workRequiresHold = false;')])
